cycle 4, operator sign-off 2026-09-09, "Authorise the one-line client-vue
fix").

Assertion it attacks: the SEQUENCE on the wire, not a single click — driving
one status tile (click A), then a second (click B), then de-selecting the
first (click A again) must leave `translateQuery(schema, model())`'s
`filter[status.code|in]` carrying ONLY the still-selected value (click B's),
with no duplicate entries anywhere in the array at any step. A prior version
of this patch attacked the single-click write landing at all ("wires
status.code|in and category.slug|in for what was actually clicked"); that
assertion is too weak for THIS cycle's defect — one click passed clean for
three prior cycles while the SEQUENCE was broken underneath it, because a
single click never exercises a diff against prior selection.

PROVING ASSERTION EXISTS YET: the permanent gate is
`packages/client-vue/src/components/form/renderers/__tests__/invoices-filter-wire.test.ts`,
which the prover is extending in parallel with a two-click-plus-de-select
sequence assertion over the same dotted `status.code` column this file's
existing single-click test already drives (coordinated by contract, not by
editing that file here).

Mutation: restores the pre-cycle-4 diff-based write — `current` re-read off
`multiEnumControl.control.value.data` and the next selection replayed as a
computed `difference(next, current)` / `difference(current, next)` pair
through `addItem`/`removeItem`, instead of dispatching the whole `next`
selection as one literal-path `update`. `control.value.data` resolves to
`undefined` for this column PERMANENTLY (`@jsonforms/core`'s own
`composeWithUi` re-joins the scope's segments with "." and `Resolve.data`
splits that string back on "." — a schema property with a literal dot in its
name, `"status.code"`/`"category.slug"`, is walked as two nested keys that do
not exist), so `current` is always `[]`: every click re-adds every
already-selected item (`difference(next, []) === next`) and no click ever
computes a removal (`difference([], next) === []`). Verified by hand before
filing this control (developer seat, source-read; the prover verifies the RED
blind per `agent-seat-separation.companion.md`): applying this mutation to
the fixed source and driving click A / click B / click A again through
`filter.harness.ts`'s `mountFilters` reproduces the reported wire VERBATIM —
`"invoice_adjusted"` → `"invoice_adjusted,invoice_adjusted,invoice_cancelled"`
→ `"invoice_adjusted,invoice_adjusted,invoice_cancelled,invoice_cancelled"`.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

